{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-apu-single-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.41, step 7f: `process-apu-single`, Total Energy Consumption from AUXILIARY POWER (9191) for the combination long-haul truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, from the default database plus the run's county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-hotelling.esm`, the same as `process-extended-idle-single`'s).\n\nTWO PROCESSES COME OUT OF ONE SELECTION. The RunSpec selects 9191; MOVES's Go BaseRateCalculator rewrites a process-91 block at operating mode 203, shore power, to process 93 'Hotelling Shore Power' (baseratecalculator.go:1021-1037), so the output carries 41 diesel APU rows (mode 201) and 50 shore-power rows (diesel and the 9 CNG model years with a 203 rate). The model splits the rate at the mode (`rtDay_meanBaseRate` keeps the APU's modes, `rtDay_meanBaseRateShorePower` the retagged one), scales each by its own hourFractionAdjust from the merged hotellingActivityDistribution at zone 261610 -- 201's and 203's opModeFraction, and 1 for CNG, which the county states no row for -- and ranks the process-93 pairs after the own ones (`spc_*`). Activity and road type are extended idle's.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 91. `run_domainUnported` and `run_selectionUnported` are 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
